{
  "design_rationale": "Plant is positive-gain with 2-4 s pure delay + ~10 s lag, strongly nonlinear: u=0.5 flat at ~0.17 (E1), u=0.65 only moves at low level (E4), u=0.7 decays 0.43->0.37 (E9) so eq~0.37, while u=0.75 rises 0.37->0.48 in 6s (E10), 0.46->0.55 in 5s (E11), 0.56->0.61 in 3.5s (E12) and u=0.8 drives 0.39->0.52 in 5s (E6) and 0.52->0.61 in 4s (E7). Hence static gain dy/du ~5-6 between 0.7-0.8, equilibrium for 0.6 needs ~0.73-0.78, chosen FF=0.75. Observed net rate ~0.023-0.03/s at u=0.8-0.9 and drain ~-0.03/s at y~0.5 (E8: hold 2-3s then 0.62->0.45), tau~10-16s. Noise +-0.02 sd<0.03. Therefore: FF carries steady load for low energy, small P (0.28 => loop gain ~1.4 at high K but capped) + very small I (0.055 with +-0.08 authority, gated to yf>0.45 and |e|<0.3 with conditional freeze on saturation) to avoid windup during 3s delay, D on filtered y (Kd=0.8, tau_d=0.8s) to brake momentum, 1.2s measurement filter to cut noise without adding lag, progressive cap above 0.65 (0.78-2.0*(yf-0.65)) plus hard cap 0.35 above 0.80 and asymmetric slew (up 0.12/s, down 1.5/s) to respect delay momentum and 0.9 hard cutoff with 0.1 margin for unseen true state.",
  "machine_card": "Reservoir, u in [0,1] pump raises level, drains alone to near-zero. Direction: positive. Speed: net +0.023/s at u=0.8 low-mid level (E2 0.19->0.37/8s, E6 0.39->0.52/5s, E7 0.52->0.61/4s), +0.03/s at u=0.9 (E5 0.20->0.38/6s); drain -0.02 to -0.03/s at y~0.4-0.6 (E8 0.62->0.45/6s, E3 0.39->0.11/15s). Lag: 2-4s pure delay + dominant tau 8-15s (E4 flat 3s then rise, E8 holds 2-3s before falling). Dead-zone/nonlinear: u=0.5 eq ~0.17 (E1 flat), u=0.65 weak (E4), u=0.7 eq 0.36-0.38 and cannot hold 0.43 (E9), u=0.75 clearly rising at all levels (E10/E11/E12), u=0.8 eq >0.61 (E6/E7). Steady u for y=0.6 is ~0.73-0.80, best ~0.75. Self-draining: yes, to ~0.1, faster at high y, tau ~10s. Noise: zero-mean +-0.02, sd <0.02. Safety: stay <0.85 soft, 0.9 forces u=0; true state hidden so keep margin.",
  "operator_note": "Controller is slow and cautious by design. Expect gradual climb to 0.55-0.65 band within ~20-30 s and then quiet holding near u~0.75. Do not step target abruptly; noise may cause +-0.03 pump jitter which is normal. It will cut pump hard if filtered level exceeds 0.70-0.80 to protect the 0.9 cutoff.",
  "predicted_behavior": "From low level, ramp at slew-limited ~0.12/s to ~0.82, rise ~0.025/s, reach 0.55 in ~15-20s, brake via D + progressive cap, settle to 0.60 +-0.03 within ~25-35s with <0.05 overshoot and no exceedance of 0.80 true. Steady duty ~0.73-0.78 (FF 0.75 + small trim). After 30s settling: MAE ~0.015-0.025, in-band >80-90%, energy ~0.56 per step (u^2 ~0.56). From near-target start, settle in ~10-15s.",
